error[E0404]: `N` contains itself by value, so it would have no finite size
 --> mem:///main.lu:1:20
  |
1 | struct N { v: int, next: L }
  |                    ^^^^ `N` reaches itself through here: N -> L -> N
  |
  = note: a struct's fields, an enum's payloads and a tuple's elements are laid out inline, so a
    type that reaches itself through them alone would be a value with no finite size
    ([type.rec]). Recurse through a container that holds its element elsewhere: `List[N]`,
    `Map[K, N]`, or a `handle N` into a pool.
